{"op":"pr_create","base":"main","head":"feature/360-resource-optimiser-profile-first","title":"feat(#360): apply optimiser profile-first","draft":true,"body":"## Summary\n\nMakes Resource Optimiser direct apply profile-first, constraining ramp-up to the resource types selected by `countRanges` and preserving explicit capacity plans.\n\n## Related issue\n\nCloses #360\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added a dedicated optimiser-apply service that derives minimal mutations, classifies named-resource ownership, and fails closed for ambiguous or planner-managed capacity.\n- Persists eligible named-resource ramp-up as authoritative `NAMED_PERSON` / `AVAILABILITY_WINDOW` / `DERIVED` profiles, then projects compatibility fields.\n- Applies snapshots, counts, profiles, schedule, timeline entries, optional staggering, and cache invalidation in one serializable transaction.\n- Added scoped ramp-up unit coverage, profile-first service tests, PostgreSQL integration coverage, and a direct-apply Playwright scenario.\n\n## Design, data, or migration notes\n\nNo Prisma schema migration. Existing segmented, manual, duplicate, planner-managed, malformed, or otherwise ambiguous named-resource profiles produce HTTP 409 (`PROFILE_MANAGED_CAPACITY`) with actionable guidance. The profile classification is revalidated inside the serializable transaction before any mutation.\n\n## Validation\n\n**Repository validation:**\n\n```text\nnpm run validate\nPassed: client/server lint, type-checking, builds, backup and local lifecycle regression tests, server tests (1063 passed; 117 skipped), and client tests (301 passed).\n```\n\n- [x] Client and server lint passed\n- [x] Client and server type-checking passed\n- [x] Client and server builds passed\n- [x] Client and server unit/integration tests passed\n- [x] Backup regression tests passed (Linux and Windows CI)\n- [x] No unexplained failures were classified as pre-existing\n\n## Security\n\n- [x] Backup credential handling was verified (PGPASSWORD used, no credential-bearing process arguments)\n\n## E2E tests\n\n**Tests added/modified:**\n\n- `e2e/tests/timeline.spec.ts` — `apply candidate persists through the direct-apply workflow`\n\n**Result:**\n\n```text\nnpm run test:e2e:local -- --grep \"apply candidate persists through the direct-apply workflow\"\nPassed\n\nnpm run test:e2e:local\nPassed; disposable `monrad_pg_` container cleanup confirmed.\n```\n\n- [x] Playwright coverage was added/updated for changed user-visible behaviour\n- [x] `e2e/TESTS.md` was updated when Playwright coverage changed\n\n## Documentation and screenshots\n\n- [x] Relevant domain documentation is current\n- [x] Screenshots are not applicable; no material layout change\n\n## Risks and follow-ups\n\nNo schema migration. Optimiser apply intentionally rejects profile-managed ownership rather than overwriting it; users must adjust capacity through the owning workflow.\n\n## Review control\n\n- [x] This PR is ready for human review\n- [x] Auto-merge is not enabled\n- [x] The tracked issue will be closed by `Closes #360`\n\n**Do not merge — wait for review.**"}